# UNVERIFIED — pending debrief
#
# `INT64_MIN / -1` and `INT64_MIN % -1` are both undefined in C, and on arm64
# NEITHER traps: measured, the division returns INT64_MIN and the remainder
# returns 0, both at exit 0. On x86 the same program raises SIGFPE. Same source,
# two behaviours, no diagnostic — which is why `%` is guarded exactly like `/`
# even though the spec's abort list mentions only division by zero (queued as a
# spec gap).
#
# This case takes the remainder, because the division is the one everybody
# remembers.

function main()
    low: i64 @ 0 - 9223372036854775807
    low @ low - 1
    minus: i64 @ 0 - 1
    print(low % minus)
